        "original_id": "693b8679-73e7-5313-b0b3-92c8732f9d65",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nikolaas Tinbergen, Konrad Lorenz, Karl von Frisch\n- Roles: biologist, ornithologist, zoologist, ethologist\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\n- Concepts: animal behaviour, individual and social behaviour patterns\n\nFacts:\n- Konrad Lorenz was born on 7 November 1903 and died on 27 February 1989.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen was born on 15 April 1907 and died on 21 December 1988.\n- Konrad Lorenz was an Austrian zoologist, ethologist, and ornithologist.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen, also known as Niko Tinbergen, was a Dutch biologist and ornithologist.\n- In 1973, Nikolaas Tinbergen shared the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine with Karl von Frisch and Konrad Lorenz.\n- The 1973 Nobel Prize recognized discoveries by Nikolaas Tinbergen, Karl von Frisch, and Konrad Lorenz concerning the organisation and elicitation of individual and social behaviour patterns in animals.",
